{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":118122,"items":[{"abstract":"<jats:p>In 2014, R.H. Hardin contributed a family of sequences about king-moves on an array to the On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences (OEIS). The sequences were recently noticed in an automated search of the OEIS by Kauers and Koutschan, who conjectured a recurrence for one of them. We prove their conjecture as well as some older conjectures stated in the OEIS entries. We also have some new conjectures for the asymptotics of Hardin's sequences.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.37236\/12358","type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Hardinian Arrays"],"author":[{"given":"Robert","family":"Dougherty-Bliss","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Manuel","family":"Kauers","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"container-title":["The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,5]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.37236\/12358"},{"abstract":"<jats:p>\n            We resolve some open conjectures from the OEIS about Hardinian arrays (see A253217). In particular, we show via the transfer matrix method that\n            <jats:italic>\n              H\n              <jats:sub>r<\/jats:sub>\n            <\/jats:italic>\n            (\n            <jats:italic>n, k<\/jats:italic>\n            ), the number of\n            <jats:italic>n \u00d7 k<\/jats:italic>\n            Hardinian arrays with parameter\n            <jats:italic>r<\/jats:italic>\n            is a polynomial in\n            <jats:italic>n<\/jats:italic>\n            of degree\n            <jats:italic>r<\/jats:italic>\n            when\n            <jats:italic>r<\/jats:italic>\n            and\n            <jats:italic>k<\/jats:italic>\n            are fixed and\n            <jats:italic>n<\/jats:italic>\n            is sufficiently large. Our implementation of the main result in Maple and Python involves computing with large, sparse matrices, both numeric and symbolic.\n          <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1145\/3717582.3717589","type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Rectangular Hardinian Arrays"],"author":[{"given":"Robert","family":"Dougherty-Bliss","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematics, Rutgers University, Piscataway, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"George","family":"Spahn","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematics, Rutgers University, Piscataway, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"container-title":["ACM Communications in Computer Algebra"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,9]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1145\/3717582.3717589"},{"DOI":"10.1136\/bmj.316.7141.1386","title":["A Martian view of the Hardinian taboo"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[1998,5,2]]},"container-title":["BMJ"],"type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1136\/bmj.316.7141.1386"},{"DOI":"10.56702\/pjkx6569\/jspalaw_3601.14","title":["Enlightened State-Interest\u2014A Legal Framework for Protecting the \u201cCommon Interest of All Mankind\u201d from Hardinian Tragedy"],"author":[{"given":"Nicholas D.","family":"Welly","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2010,7,1]]},"container-title":["Journal of Space Law"],"type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.56702\/pjkx6569\/jspalaw_3601.14"},{"DOI":"10.1136\/bmj.315.7120.1441","title":["To the point of farce: a martian view of the hardinian taboo\u2014the silence that surrounds population control"],"author":[{"given":"Maurice","family":"King","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Charles","family":"Elliott","sequence":"additional"